by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-01T14:48:40Z

@MatTheCat you were right about the branch, this is 8.2. It changes what end users get out of `translation:pull` rather than fixing a crash, and the dev branch is the conservative place for that. I closed #65092 in favour of this one.

While preparing the merge I hit a regression in the patch as it stood. `read()` returned an empty bag whenever the requested locales were empty and locales were configured, because `array_intersect(['en', 'fr'], [])` is empty. That path is reachable from `TranslationPullCommand::execute()`, which does `$locales = $input->getOption('locales') ?: $this->enabledLocales;` while the option has no default and `framework.enabled_locales` has no default value either, so a bare `translation:pull` arrives with `[]`. `FilteringProvider` exposes `getDomains()` but no `getLocales()`, so the command cannot compensate.

Measured with a `CommandTester`, `enabled_locales` unset, provider configured with `locales: [en, fr]` and `domains: [messages]`, `translation:pull` with no options:

 * on 8.2: `messages.de.xlf`, `messages.en.xlf`, `messages.fr.xlf`, `messages.ja.xlf`, the whole project, which is the bug you are fixing;
 * with the patch as it stood: no file at all, and the command still printed `[OK] New translations ... has been written locally`, so no signal either;
 * now: `messages.en.xlf` and `messages.fr.xlf`.

So `read()` falls back to the configured filters when it is passed none:

```php
if ($this->locales && !$locales = $locales ? array_intersect($this->locales, $locales) : $this->locales) {
```

Same shape for domains. That half is belt and braces, since both commands already fall back to `getDomains()` before calling `read()`, but it keeps the two branches consistent.

On the tests, `testReadNoConfiguredLocales` asserted that `read(['messages'], [])` returns zero catalogues, which pinned exactly the behaviour above, so that assertion had to go. What is left is the `['en']` configured, `['fr']` requested case, which is a no-match case and not a no-config one, hence the rename to `testReadNoMatchingLocales`; the no-config case is `testReadRequestedLocalesWithoutConfiguredLocales`. Same rename for the domains twin. I also swapped `assertCount(0, $bag->getCatalogue('en')->getDomains())` for an assertion on `getCatalogues()`, since `TranslatorBag::getCatalogue()` creates the catalogue when it is missing and the original assertion therefore passed on a completely empty bag. Two tests cover the fallback.

Verification: restoring `FilteringProvider.php` to the 8.2 tip while keeping the tests fails 6 of the 11, the two new ones included. Full component suite is 834 tests and 2513 assertions, green apart from a local ICU wording failure in `TranslationLintCommandTest` that reproduces on 8.2 untouched.

Rebased on 8.2 and squashed into a single commit, still yours.

